  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2z-y-6=0\\,\u27f9\\,z=\\frac{y}{2}+3\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & ={(\\frac{y}{2}+3-2)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & ={(\\frac{y}{2}+1)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+y+1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-y & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}-4y+4}{4}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =2 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a circle of radius $2\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(-1,2)$ in the $xy$-plane.",
